:R-HSA-983712  a            obo:GO_0034220 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "Ion channels mediate the flow of ions across the plasma membrane of cells. They are integral membrane proteins, typically a multimer of proteins, which, when arranged in the membrane, create a pore for the flow of ions. There are different types of ion channels. P-type ATPases undergo conformational changes to translocate ions. Ligand-gated ion channels operate like a gate, opened or closed by a chemical signal. Voltage-gated ion channels are activated by changes in electrical potential difference at the membrane (Purves, 2001; Kuhlbrandt, 2004)." ;
        rdfs:label          "Ion channel transport" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Jassal, Bijay, 2010-11-02" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Edited: Jassal, Bijay, 2010-11-02" , "Reviewed: He, Lei, 2010-11-15" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-983712" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-382551/R-HSA-382551> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

